# Build and run every example program marked runnable, and fail on any
# that does not exit 0.
#
# `go build ./...` proves the examples compile; nothing proved they
# still run. examples/parallel-spawn had been exiting 1 for some time
# while its README advertised "Exits 0", and it was found by hand
# during unrelated work rather than by a check (#852, #476).
#
# The runnable set and the reason each excluded example is excluded
# live in examples/internal/smokeset, whose own test requires every
# examples/*/main.go to appear in one column or the other — so a new
# example cannot be silently uncovered.
#
# Modes:
#
#   examples-smoke           # build and run (this is what CI runs)
#   examples-smoke --print   # dump the disposition table
#
# No credentials and no arguments are passed: every runnable example
# defaults to the scripted mock provider and opts into a real one
# behind a flag this never passes. Provider keys present in the
# environment are dropped, so the answer does not depend on whose
# machine it runs on.

set -euo pipefail
. "$(dirname "$0")/common.sh"
cd "$(repo_root)"

# The runner lives under examples/internal/smokerun, not dev/: the
# manifest is an internal package of the examples tree, and Go's
# internal rule refuses an import from dev/.
exec go run ./examples/internal/smokerun "$@"
